' AND TWO CASES THAT MAY NOT CONVERT, named here so nobody converts them later:
'   TestGitRunsWhenWorktreeOwnerDiffersFromRunAsUID mounts ONLY `.git` at
'     /app/.git — no working tree, no real workspace — to reproduce git's
'     "dubious ownership" abort under a uid mismatch. A real run always mounts a
'     full workspace and never constructs that partial shape, so there is no
'     launch to convert it into.
'   TestClaudecodeEntrypointOperatesOnTheInputDir depends on PROVEO_SMOKE_TEST,
'     a self-check built into entrypoint.sh that no `proveo run` flag reaches.
' The rule the pair draws: a replica is legitimate exactly when it constructs a
' shape the product cannot, and illegitimate when it merely re-spells one the
' product already builds.
'
' Both are now SKIPPED as well, and the two rules stack rather than collide. They
' may not convert, because no launch builds their shape; and they may not run,
' because the shape they build by hand is a `docker run`. What survives is the
' record of why each exists, which is the only part a reader ever needed — the
' day either question comes back, it comes back on sbx.
'
' ── A PANE IS AN ECHO CHAMBER: NEVER WAIT ON TEXT YOU TYPED ────────────────
' HISTORY for the helpers named here (deleted 2026-10-17 — kitRun.exec reads a
' real exit status through `sbx exec`, so no marker exists to misread). The
' three rules still bind any probe that reads a pane.
' Measured 2026-09-15. shellExec typed `bash -c '<script>'; echo <marker>=$?` and
' then waited for `<marker>=` as a plain substring. The pane shows INPUT as well
' as output, so the wait was satisfied by the terminal's echo of the command —
' the same instant it was sent, before bash ran a line of the script. The screen
' it returned held only the typed line, whose trailing `=$?` parsed as no status,
' and the -1 fallback dressed that up as an answer. Every tmux-driven test in the
' suite failed at once, each blaming the thing it was probing: git unwritable in
' all five harnesses, no scope mode usable, no worktree usable, docker access
' missing everywhere. One broken probe, thirty-odd false verdicts, and nothing in
' the output pointing at the probe.
'
' Three rules, and the second is why this took a whole suite to notice:
'   5. A completion marker must be UNSPELLABLE by the input that requests it.
'      `echo '<head>''<tail>'=$?` keeps the quote characters between the halves on
'      the typed line and leaves the shell's echo the only place the marker
'      appears whole. clone_output_test.go already knew this — it matches its
'      probe's answer by shape at column 0 "because the shell echoes the command
'      first" — so the knowledge existed and the shared helper did not have it.
'   6. A probe that cannot read its own answer must FAIL, not return a sentinel.
'      `status := -1` made a broken probe indistinguishable from a command that
'      ran and failed. markerStatus returns (int, bool) and shellExec fatals on
'      false, so the next time this breaks it says so in one line.
'   7. A FIXED SLEEP IS A TIMING ASSUMPTION ABOUT ONE BACKEND, so wait on the
'      marker instead. TestAgentSettingsPersistAcrossRuns slept 4s for the shell
'      and 2s for the answer; both were long enough on the docker rendering and
'      neither was on the sandbox one, so the pane was captured holding the
'      typed line and no answer. An empty tier read as a cache that had failed
'      to re-enter — the test accused the mechanism it exists to protect. It
'      then waited through waitForContainerShell and shellExec; it now waits
'      for opencode's "Ask anything" prompt and ends the run (killAndAwait).
'      Each returns when the work is done rather than when a clock says so.
'
' A credential the AGENT cannot spend is a condition of the host, not a defect, so
' the watcher's Fatalf turns a pane matching credentialUnavailable into a SKIP with
' the diagnostics attached. That pattern is deliberately narrow — `credit balance
' is too low`, `insufficient credits|quota|balance`, `authentication_error`,
' `invalid x-api-key`, `invalid api key` — because broadening it to any early exit
' would let a real adapter defect leave as a skip.
'
' HISTORY (deleted 2026-10-17; awaitKit now waits on the sandbox name and the
' seed's /dev/shm/proveo-seed-done instead of a shell prompt).
' Two waits carry the same reasoning. waitForContainerShell treated the agent
' prompt as the signal that the WHOLE launch came up — sandbox, Kit, template
' load — because proveo only hands the PTY over once the sandbox is running, so
' anything failing earlier fails HERE with the scrollback attached rather than as a
' confusing timeout further down. It matches the PROMPT'S SHAPE, `…@host:workdir`
' followed by `$` or `#` at end of line, never a literal workdir, and never "$ ":
' tmux trims trailing whitespace, so a space-suffixed match never fires.
'
' Matching a literal ":/app$" was the whole reason seven tests read as hung.
' Measured 2026-09-15 across one run, both backends draw a prompt and neither is
' wrong:
'
'   docker   `I have no name!@8101a68d15b5:/app$`
'   sandbox  `claude@proveo-1789458382-46514:003$`
'            `opencode@proveo-1789459221-51842:001$`
'
' sbx runs the shell with the workspace at its own host path, so bash renders the
' BASENAME — `001`, `003` — and a matcher looking for the string "/app" cannot
' fire however long it waits. The prompts were on screen the entire time; four
' OpenCodeAuth legs each burned a 4-minute deadline staring at one.
' acceptChoicePrompt anchors on the key hint
' ("enter accept", 90s) rather than the form's title: the title is copy, it has been
' reworded once, and that reword broke a test that waited on it.
'
' ── TEARDOWN IS SHARED STATE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
' The suite used to call `proveo clean --force`, which removes EVERY proveo
' container AND every per-run state dir under the operator's real
' ~/.local/state/proveo/egress, live or not. On 2026-09-29 it deleted the
' home-files dirs of two live operator sandboxes (proveo-claudecode-8abaedd2 and
' -36915573), which sbx then refused to start ("workspace directory … no longer
' exists on the host"). cleanLeftovers therefore runs `proveo clean` WITHOUT
' --force, so anything that looks live — a sibling still coming up, or the
' operator's run — is kept, under a throwaway PROVEO_STATE_ROOT (PROVEO_EGRESS_ROOT
' until F17, 2026-10-17; the old name is still read with a deprecation warning), so no real
' run's state dir is ever a candidate. HISTORY: cleanLeftoversIfCrowded waited
' for cleanThreshold = 10 `proveo.egress.session` containers before sweeping;
' neither it nor cleanLeftovers is in e2e/ any more (MEASURED 2026-10-16), and
' sandboxes are swept by sweepSandboxesAfter below.
'
' ── AND SANDBOXES ARE SHARED STATE NEITHER KEY SWEEPS ──────────────────────
' Measured 2026-09-15. This is the INTERACTION of two decisions, neither wrong on
' its own. A sandbox is named for its def AND its workspace
' (_spec/internal/sbx/sandbox-backend.puml) so that a second run re-attaches
' instead of building another VM — and this suite hands every test its own
' `t.TempDir()` workspace. Def+workspace keying therefore yields NO reuse here:
' each test still builds a VM of its own, and the saving the key exists for is
' exactly the saving a suite cannot collect.
'
' sbx sizes an undeclared sandbox at half the HOST rather than half of what is
' left (the Memory note in sandbox-backend.puml), so a handful alive at once
' oversubscribes the machine. A 48 GiB host went OOM, the kernel killed the test
' binary 108 assertions in, and 19 sandboxes survived the process that made them.
' The suite reported a truncated run, not a resource fault.
'
' `sweepSandboxesAfter` closes it, hooked into `harnessImage` so every case that
' resolves a harness gets it. Three properties, each deliberate:
'   * it removes only sandboxes the TEST could have made: absent when the test
'     started AND with a primary workspace under the process temp root
'     (sbxSandboxNames reads `sbx ls --json`). "Absent at start" alone was not
'     ownership: on 2026-09-29 an operator started `proveo run` in
'     ~/Projects/pluvo/worktrees/dev while TestGitIsWritableInEveryHarness ran,
'     and its cleanup `sbx rm --force`d proveo-claudecode-1b3fcb7f mid-session
'     ("sandbox … was stopped"). And `sbx ls` was measured returning an EMPTY
'     table with exit 0 under that load, which made every sandbox "new". A
'     listing that fails skips the sweep; TestSweepNeverClaimsAnOperatorSandbox
'     pins the ownership rule;
'   * it is registered BEFORE the tmux session's Kill, because cleanups run LIFO
'     and the session has to die before the VM underneath it;
'   * its failures are IGNORED, since proveo's own teardown already removes most
'     of these and a sweep that reddens a passing test is worse than the leak it
'     was added to prevent.
'
' ── THE ENVIRONMENT A SUITE HANDS ITS CHILD ─────────────────────────────────
' Three traps, all of which present as "the session started and printed nothing":
'   * env(1) on BSD/macOS requires every -u option BEFORE any NAME=value operand,
'     so the -u list has to come first or env tries to exec "-u" as the utility and
'     the session dies with no output.
'   * Overriding HOME hides ~/.docker and with it the active context, so the CLI
'     silently falls back to /var/run/docker.sock and every docker call — starting
'     with the image pull — hangs. Pin the endpoint explicitly: dockerHost reads
'     $DOCKER_HOST, else `docker context inspect`.
'   * ISOLATE PROVEO_HOME, NOT HOME, when what the test needs is proveo's own
'     settings out of the way. HOME is where every OTHER tool on the host keeps
'     its state as well, and sbx is one of them: overriding it moves sbx's own
'     state directory, and the run then dies at `sbx template load` against a
'     store it cannot see — reported, like every early death on this backend, as
'     "session exited before the agent shell". Measured 2026-09-15 on
'     TestAgentSettingsPersistAcrossRuns, which had isolated HOME since it was
'     written and only broke when the sandbox backend became the default. The
'     docker-endpoint trap above is the same shape, and PROVEO_HOME avoids it
'     too. What still needs a whole isolated HOME — a harness CLI's own config —
'     must pin DOCKER_HOST alongside it.
'   * An isolated proveo home is also what makes driving the choice prompt
'     deterministic. A shared one would leak into the developer's real settings
'     AND skip the prompt on every later run.
' ── FOUR FIXTURE FAULTS, FIXED 2026-10-20 ───────────────────────────────────
' Each failed a case for a reason outside its subject. The failing output is
' reported from the Executor's run; no sbx ran where the fixes were written.
'   * IDLE: A WORKSPACE WITH A DEPENDENCY TREE IS A COMMITTED REPO.
'     idleWorkspace (e2e/idle_test.go) is the shape that died at ~16s: go.mod
'     (gopls / go mod download) plus a package.json with no engines.node (the
'     node-version lookup). An empty TempDir never reached that seed path, so
'     the idle gate passed while `proveo run cursor` against this repo did not.
'     The fixture was a plain TempDir. decideClone (internal/run/run.go)
'     answered "not a git repository", so launchSandbox's mounted-checkout
'     preflight refused the package.json tree; DepCopies counts a marker's
'     dirs whether or not they exist (internal/workspace/deps.go, MEASURED).
'     proveo exited, and the next pty write failed with `write /dev/ptmx:
'     input/output error` on every target (reported). The fixture now runs
'     gitInit, and the run passes `--clone`: a host PROVEO_CLONE=off then
'     fails loudly (CloneSet) instead of reopening the mounted path.
'     The prompt loop checks `exited` BEFORE reachedPromptFor. proveo's own
'     plan line `agent: <target> <version> — pinned at build` matched a prompt
'     marker, so a dead run read as a live prompt (reported).
'     reachedPromptFor also drops that one line (withoutPlanLine).
'     [Inference] opencode's and cecli's markers are their bare names, which
'     other proveo lines may carry; for them the `exited` check is the guard.
'     RESIDUAL: e2e/ladder_test.go still checks the marker before `exited`.
'   * WORKTREE: A FIXTURE THE SEED INSTALLS INTO CARRIES ITS LOCKFILE.
'     newTempWorktree (e2e/scope_mounts_test.go) committed a package.json and
'     no lockfile. The seed's _dep_install_cmd (packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh)
