'                         PROVEO_SIGNAL_TEST=1 gate left `proveo-dev e2e-full`)
'   a docker home ....... TestOpenCodeTwoSessionsSurviveProveoRuns
'                         (opencode_sessions_test.go, pinned PROVEO_SBX=0)
'   the consent gate .... ReviewTierConsentGate
'   the fallback itself . SandboxBackendFallsBackToDockerWhenSbxAbsent, now the
'                         refusal TestSandboxBackendRefusesWhenSbxAbsent
'                         (TestRetiredSbxOffValuesRefuseTheRun lived one day; its
'                         stub went with "Drop all four", 2026-10-17)
'   raw docker replicas . GitRunsWhenWorktreeOwnerDiffersFromRunAsUID ·
'                         ClaudecodeEntrypointOperatesOnTheInputDir ·
'                         toolchain's runLib · ToolchainLibIsCurrentInEveryHarness
'
' AND ONE THAT CHANGED SUBJECT: TestCursorEgressException asserted a CLI
' refusal (`--egress-mode allowlist` declined, naming `open`). With cursor's
' `egress: [open]` and `credentials: [forward]` pins dropped ("Drop the pins")
' it became TestCursorBrokersThroughTheSbxStore: cursor's key goes to sbx's
' secret store, never a bare `-e`. A test is a docker subject when the
' RENDERING is what it reads, not when the word "egress" appears in it.
'
' HISTORY — "SKIPPED, NOT DELETED". From 2026-09-15 each retired probe began
' with `skipOutsideSbx(t, subject)`, on the argument that a skipped case keeps
' the question its probe measured. That rule held while the docker rendering
' shipped. Once the Executor deleted the rendering, a skipped probe of it would
' measure nothing that exists, so the cases were deleted with their subject and
' skipOutsideSbx is gone from e2e/ (MEASURED). The record of what each measured
' is the list above. e2e/go-testing-standards.md states the suite rules for the
' people writing these tests.
'
' The sweep narrows with it: TestImageMitmproxy and the Layer-3 task
' (`test-go-integration`) are deleted. Since N12 (2026-10-17, MEASURED) ONE
' `test-images` task runs every TestImage* suite — hermes included — and both
' `test-e2e` and `test-e2e-full` depend on it (mise.toml:79,97,103;
' TestOneImageTaskGatesBothReleaseGates). HISTORY: test-images-sbx ran a regex
' of five suites, which skipped TestImageHermes and TestImageDetachedSmoke.
'
' ── AND SO PROVEO_SBX=off MEANS NOTHING ─────────────────────────────────────
' There is no backend to pin it to. PROVEO_SBX off values hard-failed every
' `proveo run` for one day (2026-10-16); since 2026-10-17 ("Drop all four") the
' variable is simply unread (_spec/internal/sbx/sandbox-backend.puml). The last
' test that pinned it, e2e/opencode_sessions_test.go (PROVEO_SBX=0, docker path
' only), was deleted 2026-10-16. HISTORY of the ban: no e2e test could pin
' the backend off. The pin was introduced so a probe could inspect the docker
' rendering — the "-egress" container, the broker.env bound into it, a mount
' table — without waiting out a timeout on a host where sbx takes the run. It
' worked, and that was the problem: on a host with sbx installed, the backend
' the OPERATOR gets was the one rendering nothing asserted. The suite certified
' a shape the machine does not run.
'
' The rule above answers that by removing the reason to reach for the pin at
' all. Where a case survives because its subject is not the rendering, two
' techniques still apply, and they are now refinements rather than a ladder:
'   1. Assert the BEHAVIOUR, not the rendering. "git history is writable from
'      inside the harness" is a claim about the harness and holds on sbx;
'      "tracked.txt from the host mount is committable" holds only under
'      docker, because sbx clones committed history and the untracked file
'      never crosses. The second is a docker fact wearing a git claim —
'      rewrite the probe to create its own file and the claim is about the
'      harness again.
'   2. HISTORY: BRANCH on what the run resolved, the way assertPlanIsolation
'      branched on isSbxArgv. With one backend there is nothing to branch on;
'      a host that cannot run sbx now refuses `--print` outright.
' The third technique this list used to carry — skip on the other rendering
' where a mechanism exists in one only — is not a technique any more. It is
' the default, and the governing rule states it.
'
' Where the provider must be detected from a workspace .env alone, the test unsets
' every provider Detect variable but PRESERVES infrastructure ones such as
' DOCKER_HOST, which may point at a remote daemon.
'
' ── WHAT THE CREDENTIAL SUITE ASSERTS, AND OVER WHAT VALUES ─────────────────
' Every value is random per run (`tst_` + 24 random bytes, hex), so no real secret
' is involved and a leak is unambiguous; a mismatch is reported as sha256 prefix +
' length, never by printing the key. Two complementary halves, and the sbx-only
' rule above cut between them rather than through either:
'   * isolation (every agent, deterministic) — one `--print` subtest per agent
'     (TestCredentialForwardingIntegrity). The dry-run builds the sbx argv
'     through the exact same env code path as a real run, so it is faithful and
'     starts no VM — but it needs a ready sbx, since `--print` refuses without
'     one. It asserts no raw key value and no `KEY=` pair in argv.
'   * cursor — TestCursorBrokersThroughTheSbxStore: cursor's key is named for
'     sbx's secret store and never rides argv as a bare `-e CURSOR_API_KEY`.
'   Both halves run their `--print` child under a fresh PROVEO_HOME
'   (printEnforcedPlan, runPrint); CREDENTIALS under FOUR FIXTURE FAULTS says why.
' HISTORY, deleted 2026-10-16 with the docker rendering: the live "egress
' integrity" half (one firewall run whose broker.env, bind-mounted into the
' egress-proxy, had to receive each key byte-for-byte; claudecode drove it
' because providers:[anthropic] is what armed the broker), the project-.env
' variant (a key only in the workspace .env reached the sidecar while the agent
' saw the sentinel and an EMPTY /app/.env), and cursor's `--egress-mode
' allowlist` refusal ("allowed: open").
'
' ── WHY SOME LAYER-4 CASES HAVE NO CONTAINER AT ALL ─────────────────────────
' `proveo init --print` is the one mode that must be safe on any host: it resolves
' the plan and reports this machine's verdict without downloading, installing,
' signing in, or writing anything. Running it against the REAL host is the only way
' to catch a plan that resolves fine in a table test but names a path or a distro
' that does not exist here — and the assertion is symmetric, checking both that the
' output names the pinned release / the asset / the host triple AND that the prefix
' was never created and nothing was left in the working directory. The provenance
' case is Layer 4 for the same reason: the digest is fetched from the LIVE release
' at install time, so a bumped Release with a moved subject name would only fail on
' a host nobody is watching. Details of what init plans are in
' _spec/cmd/proveo/init-sbx-bootstrap.puml.
'
' ── THE INVOCATIONS, AS THE SUITES THEMSELVES RECORD THEM ───────────────────
'   go test -tags=e2e ./e2e/ -run CredentialForwardingIntegrity -v
'   go test -tags=e2e ./e2e/ -run SandboxBackendRefuses -v
'   [PROVEO_TEST_LOCAL_MODEL=gemma4] \
'     go test -tags=e2e ./e2e/ -run PromptfulE2E -v -timeout 360s
'   go test -tags=e2e ./e2e/ -run InitPrint -v
'   go test -tags=e2e ./e2e/ -run InitProvenance -v

