note right of L1
  Host orchestration under test is **Go**
  (""cmd/proveo"", ""internal/{workspace,run,
  sbx,gitidentity,manifest}""). Fat bash runners and the
  ""defs/lib/egress.sh"" lifecycle are retired.
end note

note right of L2
  **Go-first contracts:** execute the builders and diff
  the argv/plan, rather than grepping source for literal
  strings. A grep contract survives the deletion of the
  thing it claimed to test — it passes while testing
  nothing. Image suites are Go too (-tags=image).
end note

note right of L4
  **sbx is the runtime under test, and the only
  one.** The docker rendering and its probes were
  deleted 2026-10-16; a restated image tag still
  stops matching the day the tag policy moves.
end note

note as SBXONLY
  **Scope and product now agree.** The mitmproxy
  sidecar and the docker fallback no longer ship,
  so no case needs a scope skip to stay honest
  about a runtime the operator never receives.
end note

note as SKIPNOTDELETE
  **Skipped kept the question while its subject
  shipped.** Once the subject was deleted, the
  probe was deleted with it; the list of what
  each measured is the record that remains.
end note

note right of L3
  **Retired with its subject.** It stood up the
  docker egress topology (""BuildPlan"" +
  ""ExecRunner""): MITM, Squid, broker.env. Its
  practices — wait on a condition, ""t.Cleanup"",
  a named skip — live on in Layer 4.
end note

note right of L4
  **Two lanes, keyless.** ""e2e_test.go"" runs
  opencode on a local Ollama model and
  ""hello_world_test.go"" runs all three targets
  on one, supplying no provider credential.
  Both assert side effects, not the model's prose.
end note

note bottom of COV
  Default ""go test ./..."" never compiles Layer 4 or the
  image suites — the PR path stays fast and keyless. No
  hard coverage gate until a baseline exists; CI
  publishes the percent as an artifact. The Stage 0b
  egress-proxy cover image went with Layer 3.
end note

