note as ECHOAGENT
  **The Layer-4 promptful E2E runs against a fixture agent, not a vendor
  CLI.** ""defs/tests/echo-agent"" is a minimal image that reads a prompt and
  calls the local model through the OpenAI-compatible endpoint
  ""--local-model"" already provides — so the suite exercises proveo's own
  wiring (mounts, egress, model routing) without a paid API key or a
  vendor's release cadence in the loop.
end note


note as VACUOUS1
  **A test that cannot fail is worse than a
  missing one.** claudecode's helpers never
  defined ""run_timeout"", so the pipeline that
  called it produced ""0"" from ""grep -c"" and the
  assertion PASSED without starting a container.
end note

note as VACUOUS2
  **Put a positive assertion first.** Two
  ""assert_failure"" checks aimed at a retired
  path: ""grep"" found no directory, failed, and
  both reported PASS having verified nothing.
end note

note as VACUOUS3
  **A suite must not build what it tests.**
  claudecode's phase 1 ran a bare ""docker
  build"", so the Dockerfile's PUBLISHED default
  base applied and overwrote the local lineage —
  surfacing as ""bun: command not found"".
end note

note as VACUOUS4
  **One missing function ended nine phases.**
  A ""sed"" for a helper that had already moved
  left an empty ""eval"", so the call exited 127
  and ""set -e"" took every later phase with it.
end note

note as VACUOUS5
  **Zero of N reads as all of N.** An ""sbx"" plan
  carries no key in argv, so a blind sentinel
  loop checked nothing and reported success. The
  check now asserts no value and no KEY= in argv.
end note

note as REALLAUNCH
  **Drive the product, not a replica of it.**
  Seven cases reassembled the mounts, the relay
  and the clone that ""proveo run"" constructs
  itself, so a replica could keep reporting
  success after the assembly it imitated moved.
end note

note as SHELLHELPERS
  **The probe rides ""sbx exec""; the posture is pinned.**
  kitRun.exec runs each script as its own
  ""bash -c"" in the sandbox and returns the real
  exit status; launchKit fixes the credential
  posture (was launchShell + shellExec).
end note

note as SEEDEDCHOICE
  **Seed the choice; never drive the checkboxes.**
  An isolated agentsettings.Store brings the real
  form up already ticked, so a case asserting on
  an add-on is not simultaneously asserting on
  the picker's key bindings, which have moved.
end note

note as NOREPLICA
  **A replica is legitimate only for a shape the
  product cannot build.** One case mounts a bare
  "".git"" to provoke a dubious-ownership abort
  and another depends on PROVEO_SMOKE_TEST, which
  no ""proveo run"" flag reaches; both stay raw.
end note

note as SANDBOXSWEEP
  **Two sound keys, one leak.** Def+workspace
  naming buys reuse an operator wants, but every
  test here owns a fresh ""t.TempDir()"", so each
  builds its own VM at half the host — 48 GiB
  went OOM and nineteen sandboxes outlived it.
end note

note as PREREQ
  **Skip only for a missing prerequisite.** The
  ""e2e"" tag is the opt-in, so a green run with every
  test skipped is an honest statement about the
  host — and ""go test -v"" prints each reason.
end note

note as DIAGNOSE
  **Snapshot while the session is alive.** Capturing
  at the moment of failure returns 'no server
  running' and hides the exit output. Only 4 empty
  captures in a row mean dead, and ""docker ps -a""
  separates 'started and died' from 'never started'.
end note

note as DELIVERYROUTES
  **Both routes deliver; the sandbox delivers
  late.** Teardown writes the agent's commits to
  ""refs/proveo/<sid>/"" after the tmux session
  has gone, so an assertion taken at that moment
  finds nothing and blames the product.
end note

note as RUNLOGCAP
  **Capture proveo's own log before the temporary
  home disappears.** That file is the sole account
  of an early termination the pane could not
  retain, and the framework removes the directory
  containing it when the test finishes.
end note

note as NOSLEEP
  **A fixed sleep encodes one backend's timing.**
  Four seconds for the shell and two for the
  answer satisfied the docker rendering but not
  the sandbox, so an empty capture was reported
  as a persistence failure in the choice cache.
end note

note as PROVEOHOME
  **Isolate PROVEO_HOME, not HOME.** Overriding
  HOME relocates every other tool's state
  directory as well, and sbx is one of them: the
  run then dies at ""sbx template load"" against a
  store it cannot see, reported as an early exit.
end note

note as TAGPICK
  **Prefer the local tag, then the published one.**
  Naming one skipped whole suites on a machine that
  had just built the thing under test — or ran the
  PUBLISHED image while the report read as local.
end note

note as ROSTER
  **Read the roster from the image.**
  A list restated in a test drifts the moment
  the roster moves: cursor and opencode logged
  10 failures against a correctly built image,
  which reads as a broken image, not a stale test.
end note

note as DEFTESTS
  **Each def has its own image suite** in ""internal/imagetest"", and they
  share one framework: ""imagetest.Suite"" runs a command inside the built
  image and asserts on its output, one subtest per check. A context
  deadline bounds every docker call, so no host ""timeout""/""gtimeout""
  binary is needed — macOS ships neither by default.

  Two habits worth keeping when editing them. The entrypoint is exercised
  by mounting a fixture project and **short-circuiting the final exec**
  (an unsupported flag that exits immediately), so a TUI launch does not
  hang a test. And several assertions have to tolerate the harness CLI
  normalising its own config on launch — cursor rewrites
  ""~/\.cursor/cli-config\.json"" every start and backs up an invalid one as
  ""\.bad"", so a test asserting on a config file must account for the CLI
  having touched it.
end note


